1
00:00:00,710 --> 00:00:04,850
<i>A skeleton dating 200 years back
found in the Himalayas,</i>

2
00:00:04,850 --> 00:00:08,520
<i>matched with the DNA
of his missing step-sister.</i>

3
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:12,440
I managed to find an email
Professor Ishimizaki sent to Kayoko Senba.

4
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:16,780
Shiharu is involved in this sin of his.

5
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:22,000
This is...

6
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:26,620
Even if you managed to find your sister,

7
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:29,550
I would simply devour her.

8
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,790
Sir.

9
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:08,200
Your visitor has arrived.

10
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:09,620
Let her through.

11
00:01:19,270 --> 00:01:23,230
Good evening. To what do I owe the pleasure?

12
00:01:23,230 --> 00:01:26,870
Can you not even monitor your own son?

13
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:29,450
I see.

14
00:01:29,450 --> 00:01:30,700
So he visited you.

15
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:33,290
Don't "I see" me.

16
00:01:37,770 --> 00:01:42,710
You killed Ishimizaki, did you not?

17
00:01:46,230 --> 00:01:47,750
I did.

18
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:52,040
And you...

19
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:55,420
are my accomplice.

20
00:02:25,890 --> 00:02:30,020
I had no hand in his death.

21
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:32,680
What are you accusing me of?

22
00:02:33,310 --> 00:02:35,640
We practically killed the man ourselves.

23
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:38,620
You had ambition.

24
00:02:39,240 --> 00:02:41,750
I had my reasons.

25
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:45,390
Ishimizaki was only caught in the crossfire.

26
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:52,020
[27 Years Ago]

27
00:02:52,020 --> 00:02:53,770
Doctor.

28
00:02:53,770 --> 00:02:57,100
I found something very interesting.

29
00:02:57,100 --> 00:02:58,690
See?

30
00:02:58,690 --> 00:03:00,900
This is in very good condition.

31
00:03:00,900 --> 00:03:05,680
And there is still muscle fiber that remains.

32
00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:09,630
Thank you.

33
00:03:12,810 --> 00:03:16,300
We'll use this, Nanase.

34
00:03:17,460 --> 00:03:19,200
Understood.

35
00:03:19,910 --> 00:03:22,540
Ishimizaki, get the box ready.

36
00:03:30,270 --> 00:03:33,450
These bones are in great condition.

37
00:03:35,770 --> 00:03:37,950
Finally, we can begin.

38
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:46,150
[Haruka Nanase]

39
00:03:53,110 --> 00:03:55,380
Haruka, where are you right now?

40
00:03:56,310 --> 00:03:58,560
<i>Are you trying to get rid of me?</i>

41
00:03:58,560 --> 00:03:59,950
What?

42
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:03,820
I was nearly killed.

43
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:06,820
<i>What? Are you hurt?</i>

44
00:04:06,820 --> 00:04:09,060
I was burnt.

45
00:04:09,060 --> 00:04:11,690
He poured some sort of chemical on me.

46
00:04:11,690 --> 00:04:14,350
If he doused me in it, I'd be dead.

47
00:04:14,350 --> 00:04:17,230
Where are you? Are you safe?

48
00:04:17,230 --> 00:04:18,600
I'll send someone to get you.

49
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:21,440
You're the one after my neck!

50
00:04:21,440 --> 00:04:23,900
<i>I'm not, I swear it.</i>

51
00:04:23,900 --> 00:04:25,880
<i>Tell me, what happened?</i>

52
00:04:26,710 --> 00:04:29,480
You tried to get me admitted to a ward.

53
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:31,150
I heard.

54
00:04:31,150 --> 00:04:33,440
The doctor deemed it was best for you.

55
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:36,350
Really, the doctor?

56
00:04:36,350 --> 00:04:39,190
I know it was your plan all along.

57
00:04:39,190 --> 00:04:41,970
<i>You think the doctor was acting on my orders?</i>

58
00:04:42,550 --> 00:04:45,850
And now you're trying to kill me instead.

59
00:04:45,850 --> 00:04:48,770
Calm down. There's been a misunderstanding.

60
00:04:48,770 --> 00:04:50,690
Tell me where you are.

61
00:04:50,690 --> 00:04:54,050
You're in grave danger right now.

62
00:04:54,810 --> 00:04:57,510
That's your fault.

63
00:04:57,510 --> 00:04:59,910
<i>I'm telling you, you misunderstand.</i>

64
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:06,250
Tell that to the man named Ushio.

65
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:11,000
I know he also killed Professor Ishimizaki.

66
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:15,040
<i>I would never do anything to hurt you.</i>

67
00:05:15,660 --> 00:05:17,610
<i>It's true, so please.</i>

68
00:05:17,610 --> 00:05:19,650
<i>Tell me where you are.</i>

69
00:05:19,650 --> 00:05:22,390
Like hell I could trust you.

70
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:25,850
What are you trying to hide?

71
00:05:25,850 --> 00:05:28,060
Is Shiharu somehow involved?

72
00:05:28,060 --> 00:05:33,030
There's still something you don't know.

73
00:05:33,030 --> 00:05:35,100
<i>And what is that?</i>

74
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:36,200
I'll tell you in person.

75
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:38,370
No. Tell me, now.

76
00:05:40,410 --> 00:05:42,610
I can't.

77
00:05:42,610 --> 00:05:44,810
Let's talk, face-to-face.

78
00:05:44,810 --> 00:05:46,800
I'd rather not.

79
00:05:57,860 --> 00:05:59,910
Failed to convince your son?

80
00:05:59,910 --> 00:06:01,550
Silence!

81
00:06:02,230 --> 00:06:05,750
If only you weren't so involved
with Plantae...

82
00:06:05,750 --> 00:06:08,060
Excuse me?

83
00:06:08,060 --> 00:06:11,910
You're the one with deep ties to Plantae.

84
00:06:14,670 --> 00:06:19,980
This all stemmed from a plan
of your father's.

85
00:06:19,980 --> 00:06:23,850
And now that it's failed,
you're trying to forget it.

86
00:06:23,850 --> 00:06:28,440
As if I could so readily accept that.

87
00:06:28,440 --> 00:06:31,620
Don't act like you alone are so righteous.

88
00:06:34,650 --> 00:06:39,050
Your son. He's getting in your way, isn't he?

89
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:43,410
Of course not.

90
00:06:47,150 --> 00:06:50,920
You must hurry
and erase all traces of "log.0".

91
00:07:55,610 --> 00:07:59,980
Haruka Nanase was reported
for breaking and entering, right?

92
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:03,150
Yes, sir. Kayoko Senba made the call.

93
00:08:03,150 --> 00:08:04,480
I see.

94
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:08,880
She also attended Ishimizaki's funeral.

95
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:10,290
So I heard.

96
00:08:10,940 --> 00:08:16,000
Maybe Haruka Nanase
is looking into Ishimizaki's case.

97
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:20,060
You think he suspects Kayoko Senba?

98
00:08:20,060 --> 00:08:23,370
There's still something he hasn't told us.

99
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:29,290
What about our other victim, Onodera?

100
00:08:31,180 --> 00:08:35,350
What was he up to
before investigating Nichie?

101
00:08:35,350 --> 00:08:37,520
Probably blackmail.

102
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:39,330
Blackmail?

103
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:44,520
He'd find disputes caused by minor companies
and hold it against them.

104
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:47,310
Money trouble, illegal subsidies, the works.

105
00:08:47,310 --> 00:08:50,950
Then he'd make them pay up
in exchange for his silence.

106
00:08:50,950 --> 00:08:53,480
Why was a man like him

107
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:57,200
pestering a major corporation
like Nichie Pharmaceutical?

108
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:08,570
What happened to your leg?

109
00:09:08,570 --> 00:09:10,310
A man splashed chemicals onto it.

110
00:09:10,310 --> 00:09:12,560
What? Who?

111
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:15,270
The bastard who attended
Kayoko Senba's lecture.

112
00:09:15,850 --> 00:09:18,200
- The police...
- Forget them. What did you find?

113
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:20,770
- But...
- Just tell me.

114
00:09:24,270 --> 00:09:27,050
I found this old article.

115
00:09:29,850 --> 00:09:31,550
Roopkund?

116
00:09:31,550 --> 00:09:33,250
Look here.

117
00:09:34,020 --> 00:09:35,660
That's...

118
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:43,650
My uncle, your father,

119
00:09:43,650 --> 00:09:47,810
and Kayoko Senba were at Roopkund.

120
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:50,980
<i>Have you heard of Roopkund?</i>

121
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:55,190
<i>I believe so.</i>

122
00:09:55,190 --> 00:09:59,540
I wonder what it is they were investigating.

123
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:08,150
I'll go see Kayoko Senba.

124
00:10:08,150 --> 00:10:10,160
You should leave. It'll be dangerous.

125
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:11,900
We ought to report this.

126
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:14,150
The police suspect me.

127
00:10:14,150 --> 00:10:16,730
I want to talk to Kayoko Senba
before I'm caught.

128
00:10:16,730 --> 00:10:19,040
I'll come with you.

129
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:23,370
Something began at that cursed lake.

130
00:10:28,940 --> 00:10:36,940
[The bones from two centuries ago
and his missing step-sister]

131
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:40,770
I heard Kayoko Senba visited.
[log.4]

132
00:10:40,770 --> 00:10:42,650
- Was there any trouble?
- No.

133
00:10:42,650 --> 00:10:44,690
Not at all.

134
00:10:46,870 --> 00:10:48,540
What of our applied technology center?

135
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:50,610
Proceed with the demolitions.

136
00:10:50,610 --> 00:10:52,970
And please, make it quick.

137
00:10:53,870 --> 00:10:55,290
Yes, sir.

138
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:02,620
See her to a meeting room.

139
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:06,240
Kasuga's here.

140
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:07,790
Can you handle her?

141
00:11:08,560 --> 00:11:10,000
Yes, sir.

142
00:11:17,350 --> 00:11:19,730
Is the President not available?

143
00:11:19,730 --> 00:11:22,850
I have been entrusted
to handle these matters myself.

144
00:11:22,850 --> 00:11:24,730
Is that so.

145
00:11:24,730 --> 00:11:26,730
Why have I been called here today?

146
00:11:29,300 --> 00:11:34,450
We wanted to confirm every last trace
of "log.0" has been done away with.

147
00:11:35,330 --> 00:11:38,910
I believe we got rid of everything back then.

148
00:11:38,910 --> 00:11:42,580
We ask that you be absolutely certain.

149
00:11:43,990 --> 00:11:48,690
None of our records remain
in your files either, yes?

150
00:11:48,690 --> 00:11:50,160
But of course.

151
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:53,150
I ask that you be absolutely certain of it.

152
00:11:53,150 --> 00:11:55,950
I've sacrificed my family for this.

153
00:11:55,950 --> 00:12:00,600
I cannot afford to trouble them any further.

154
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:07,120
We shall bring you no trouble.

155
00:12:14,570 --> 00:12:16,700
Good.

156
00:12:17,370 --> 00:12:20,580
I will leave after sitting for a bit.

157
00:12:23,810 --> 00:12:25,620
Please take your time.

158
00:12:40,310 --> 00:12:44,350
Maehara! I'm glad we caught you.

159
00:12:44,350 --> 00:12:46,020
We have a few questions.

160
00:12:46,020 --> 00:12:51,220
A reporter came to visit Mr. Nanase
the other day, yes?

161
00:12:51,220 --> 00:12:54,200
His name was "Onodera". Ring a bell?

162
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:58,570
Yes. What about him?

163
00:12:58,570 --> 00:13:01,120
He was found as a pile of bones.

164
00:13:02,600 --> 00:13:07,440
We're obviously trying to figure out why.

165
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:09,630
Mind helping us out?

166
00:13:10,150 --> 00:13:11,500
Of course.

167
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:15,810
Onodera's come to visit Nichie recently.

168
00:13:15,810 --> 00:13:19,540
This footage is from the garage here.

169
00:13:20,350 --> 00:13:23,060
Yes, and what of it?

170
00:13:23,060 --> 00:13:25,440
He's acting pretty persistent.

171
00:13:25,440 --> 00:13:27,660
What sort of questions did he ask?

172
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:32,670
I'm sorry, but I cannot disclose
information regarding the business.

173
00:13:32,670 --> 00:13:34,650
Would we need a warrant?

174
00:13:34,650 --> 00:13:37,060
I cannot say much else about it.

175
00:13:37,060 --> 00:13:40,100
Where are you headed off to?

176
00:13:40,100 --> 00:13:42,480
I'm being sent to a hospital
to deal with prescriptions.

177
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:44,970
Mr. Kyoichi treats me
like an errand boy, at best.

178
00:13:46,660 --> 00:13:50,560
There were officers in your lobby just now.

179
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:53,350
Maehara is speaking to them.

180
00:13:53,350 --> 00:13:56,770
Worry not. The police know nothing.

181
00:13:56,770 --> 00:14:00,370
<i>And you're certain nothing will leak
from your side of things?</i>

182
00:14:00,370 --> 00:14:03,200
I have erased all evidence of "log.0".

183
00:14:05,070 --> 00:14:09,100
Did you have Ushio "erase"
the now dead reporter as well?

184
00:14:11,310 --> 00:14:13,190
Nanase.

185
00:14:13,190 --> 00:14:16,750
<i>What are you planning to do with Ushio?</i>

186
00:14:18,940 --> 00:14:21,960
[Member of the Lower House, 32nd District]

187
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:32,600
You're certainly absorbed in your work.

188
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:34,410
Chief...

189
00:14:35,310 --> 00:14:38,560
The higher-ups told me
to check on my underlings.

190
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:40,390
Are you getting up to something?

191
00:14:40,390 --> 00:14:43,150
Just doing my job, sir.

192
00:14:43,150 --> 00:14:45,770
You're no rookie, bud.

193
00:14:45,770 --> 00:14:46,820
I know.

194
00:14:46,820 --> 00:14:49,700
Careful, or you'll step on a landmine.

195
00:14:49,700 --> 00:14:53,600
Yeah, I know politics
and finance can get dicey...

196
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:57,240
Right. Don't mess with the wrong gang.

197
00:14:57,240 --> 00:15:01,250
Sorry, Chief. I got to get going.

198
00:15:01,250 --> 00:15:02,550
Talk to you later.

199
00:15:02,550 --> 00:15:04,370
Sorry!

200
00:15:18,810 --> 00:15:19,490
[Yoko Kasuga]

201
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:23,460
[Chief of PR]

202
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:30,790
- Are you alright?
- Yeah.

203
00:15:31,880 --> 00:15:35,000
You really ought to leave this case.

204
00:15:36,070 --> 00:15:38,080
So you say.

205
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:40,920
It's dangerous to get more involved.

206
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:42,980
I know.

207
00:15:42,980 --> 00:15:44,320
But I can't back off now.

208
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:47,170
If you die, who will be there
when Mari returns?

209
00:15:48,270 --> 00:15:52,330
Then will you call it quits here?

210
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:56,550
Of course not.

211
00:15:57,770 --> 00:15:59,820
And neither will I.

212
00:16:03,690 --> 00:16:08,000
I'm eternally grateful to Mari.

213
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:19,110
I was never able to fit in.
At school, my jobs, wherever.

214
00:16:19,110 --> 00:16:23,200
I'm surprised to hear that. Were you bullied?

215
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:27,020
Not exactly.

216
00:16:27,020 --> 00:16:28,960
How should I put it...

217
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:33,910
You probably realize by now
I'm honest to a fault, right?

218
00:16:36,270 --> 00:16:42,000
So I struggled to join other girls
in their superficial conversations.

219
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:48,880
They would just... slowly shun me.

220
00:16:50,330 --> 00:16:53,690
But I could always tell Mari anything.

221
00:16:53,690 --> 00:16:55,950
She'd tell me everything, too.

222
00:16:57,150 --> 00:17:02,170
She's the reason I'm the person I am now.

223
00:17:12,270 --> 00:17:13,840
I'm home.

224
00:17:14,990 --> 00:17:17,150
Welcome back.

225
00:17:17,150 --> 00:17:19,690
You haven't been skipping school these days.

226
00:17:19,690 --> 00:17:22,400
Well, university is no high school.

227
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:25,520
It actually offers me a place to study.

228
00:17:25,520 --> 00:17:27,950
How is university different from high school?

229
00:17:29,370 --> 00:17:31,540
Let's see...

230
00:17:33,190 --> 00:17:37,250
No one makes fun of me for eating alone,

231
00:17:37,250 --> 00:17:40,040
or other silly things like that, for one.

232
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:43,970
Why would they anyway?

233
00:17:44,860 --> 00:17:48,980
Middle and high school
were full of confusing rules like that.

234
00:17:48,980 --> 00:17:50,560
And university is better?

235
00:17:50,560 --> 00:17:52,250
Way better.

236
00:17:52,250 --> 00:17:53,720
I see.

237
00:17:54,350 --> 00:17:57,800
We hung out more
when you were in high school.

238
00:18:01,060 --> 00:18:02,910
Now you bring your work here.

239
00:18:02,910 --> 00:18:05,560
I can't avoid doing homework.

240
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:11,110
I used to be able to tell you anything.
You'd tell me everything, too.

241
00:18:11,110 --> 00:18:13,900
I still can.

242
00:18:13,900 --> 00:18:15,940
- Really?
- Watch.

243
00:18:15,940 --> 00:18:18,850
Today for lunch, I had ginger pork.

244
00:18:18,850 --> 00:18:21,980
The special was the grilled chicken, but...

245
00:18:21,980 --> 00:18:24,080
I wasn't asking about your lunch.

246
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:27,610
What were you up to today?

247
00:18:29,350 --> 00:18:33,840
I was at home all day.

248
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:35,380
I see.

249
00:18:39,190 --> 00:18:40,990
Should we go inside?

250
00:18:40,990 --> 00:18:43,000
Yeah.

251
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:47,980
You forgot your tea.

252
00:18:47,980 --> 00:18:50,180
Whoops! Thanks.

253
00:18:56,170 --> 00:18:58,600
I got your meal, Tada.

254
00:18:58,600 --> 00:19:00,910
Thanks.

255
00:19:04,810 --> 00:19:07,200
The cheap stuff, again?

256
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:10,510
You only gave me 1,000 yen
for both our meals and drinks.

257
00:19:11,880 --> 00:19:13,540
What'd you get?

258
00:19:18,150 --> 00:19:20,980
- That looks good.
- I'm not sharing.

259
00:19:25,610 --> 00:19:27,560
It's pretty good.

260
00:19:27,560 --> 00:19:30,150
What did you think of Maehara?

261
00:19:30,150 --> 00:19:33,940
Right, Nichie's errand boy.

262
00:19:33,940 --> 00:19:36,400
He's a direct subordinate to the President.

263
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:41,650
According to Team Two,
Maehara's always been doing shady work.

264
00:19:41,650 --> 00:19:44,770
What, he deals with bribes?

265
00:19:44,770 --> 00:19:47,520
Most likely.

266
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:52,440
Pharmaceuticals are always competing
to create the newest drug.

267
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:55,480
He was probably in charge of buy outs, too.

268
00:19:55,480 --> 00:19:57,250
I see.

269
00:19:57,740 --> 00:20:01,100
That guy was pursuing baseball in college,

270
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:03,600
until a certain scandal broke out.

271
00:20:03,600 --> 00:20:07,810
One of his teammates claimed
an upperclassman was abusing him.

272
00:20:07,810 --> 00:20:13,160
Maehara wasn't directly involved,
but the incident ruined his career.

273
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:16,900
He was treated the same
as those who were guilty.

274
00:20:16,900 --> 00:20:21,590
No company hired him,
until the Nichie President took him in.

275
00:20:21,590 --> 00:20:24,020
So that's why Maehara can't go against him?

276
00:20:24,020 --> 00:20:26,420
Yeah, he feels indebted to the guy.

277
00:20:37,690 --> 00:20:39,150
Was anyone scheduled to visit?

278
00:20:39,150 --> 00:20:40,790
No.

279
00:20:42,960 --> 00:20:46,100
[Nichie Pharmaceutical Applied Tech Center]

280
00:20:47,980 --> 00:20:50,540
Run!

281
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:52,160
Wait!

282
00:20:55,280 --> 00:20:58,000
Maehara, who were those men?

283
00:21:00,660 --> 00:21:02,770
They're most likely with Xin Ming Ah.

284
00:21:02,770 --> 00:21:04,330
Get rid of all other paper evidence.

285
00:21:04,330 --> 00:21:06,010
Yes, sir.

286
00:21:07,980 --> 00:21:13,190
The man who arrived was with Nichie.

287
00:21:13,190 --> 00:21:17,290
To visit a defunct lab... How strange.

288
00:21:18,020 --> 00:21:24,760
There was definitely something there
they didn't want us finding.

289
00:21:27,910 --> 00:21:30,440
<i>All forces, listen up!</i>

290
00:21:30,440 --> 00:21:34,360
<i>We got a witness report of Haruka Nanase.</i>

291
00:21:34,360 --> 00:21:36,260
Got you now, Haruka Nanase.

292
00:21:36,260 --> 00:21:38,600
<i>He was last seen at Terano Shopping Street.</i>

293
00:21:38,600 --> 00:21:40,600
We're rolling out.

294
00:21:40,600 --> 00:21:42,140
Yes, sir.

295
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:47,720
Once we question Kayoko Senba,
let's return to the Professor's place.

296
00:21:48,440 --> 00:21:50,370
Do you think we can get inside?

297
00:21:50,370 --> 00:21:53,820
Yes. I have the keys.

298
00:21:53,820 --> 00:21:57,100
He may have a clue regarding Roopkund.

299
00:21:57,100 --> 00:21:59,940
Something the police missed.

300
00:21:59,940 --> 00:22:01,890
Right.

301
00:22:06,580 --> 00:22:08,100
- Let's go.
- Huh?

302
00:22:08,100 --> 00:22:10,640
Hey, wait! Haruka Nanase!

303
00:22:13,810 --> 00:22:15,700
Mayuzumi, take the car and ambush them!

304
00:22:15,700 --> 00:22:17,200
Yes, sir!

305
00:23:04,860 --> 00:23:06,700
What now?

306
00:23:13,050 --> 00:23:15,700
Will you come with us to the station,

307
00:23:15,700 --> 00:23:17,870
Haruka Nanase?

308
00:23:42,230 --> 00:23:44,130
Murderer!

309
00:23:47,290 --> 00:23:50,580
That man's a murderer! Run!

310
00:23:51,330 --> 00:23:53,120
Folks, please!

311
00:23:53,120 --> 00:23:55,550
Calm down!

312
00:24:00,440 --> 00:24:03,290
Excuse me, let me through!

313
00:24:10,040 --> 00:24:13,640
He has a dangerous chemical! Watch out!

314
00:24:17,120 --> 00:24:19,000
Police!

315
00:24:30,070 --> 00:24:31,830
What happened?

316
00:24:42,950 --> 00:24:46,000
You're coming with us.

317
00:25:01,670 --> 00:25:07,850
[The Plantae Gathering]

318
00:25:07,850 --> 00:25:14,310
All who suffer must offer
their flesh and blood

319
00:25:14,310 --> 00:25:17,330
to quench thy thirst.

320
00:25:17,330 --> 00:25:23,320
All who suffer must offer
their flesh and blood

321
00:25:23,320 --> 00:25:25,910
to quench thy thirst.

322
00:25:26,530 --> 00:25:31,880
All sacrifice will one day
return to your body.

323
00:25:32,480 --> 00:25:37,620
All sacrifice will one day
return to your body.

324
00:25:39,530 --> 00:25:45,220
Like Plantae, who bear fruit
and flourish in rain.

325
00:25:45,220 --> 00:25:50,260
Like Plantae, who bear fruit
and flourish in rain.

326
00:25:50,260 --> 00:25:55,940
Rain does not choose the dry.
It supplies to all.

327
00:25:55,940 --> 00:26:01,710
Rain does not choose the dry.
It supplies to all.

328
00:26:03,150 --> 00:26:08,760
Water climbs the heavens,
till it returns to Earth.

329
00:26:08,760 --> 00:26:13,910
Water climbs the heavens,
till it returns to Earth.

330
00:26:22,950 --> 00:26:26,880
All manners occur in an eternal cycle.

331
00:26:26,880 --> 00:26:31,400
All manners occur in an eternal cycle.

332
00:26:31,400 --> 00:26:35,750
And we exist, as a part of this eternity.

333
00:26:50,310 --> 00:26:52,620
Haruka Nanase was attacked by Ushio.

334
00:26:52,620 --> 00:26:54,000
What?

335
00:26:55,060 --> 00:26:57,560
Contact the President of Nichie right away.

336
00:26:57,560 --> 00:26:59,210
Yes, ma'am.

337
00:27:03,900 --> 00:27:06,900
The new medicine has been
developed without issue.

338
00:27:06,900 --> 00:27:08,280
- Approvals are soon to be filed.
- Good.

339
00:27:08,280 --> 00:27:09,590
[J]

340
00:27:09,590 --> 00:27:11,750
- As for when...
- Pardon me.

341
00:27:16,280 --> 00:27:17,580
Hello?

342
00:27:19,100 --> 00:27:21,000
Is he hurt?

343
00:27:23,310 --> 00:27:25,460
I see.

344
00:27:27,750 --> 00:27:30,460
Who was that man?

345
00:27:31,520 --> 00:27:33,430
I don't know.

346
00:27:33,430 --> 00:27:37,310
He called himself "Ushio".

347
00:27:37,310 --> 00:27:39,000
Ushio.

348
00:27:39,780 --> 00:27:42,310
Did he say anything else?

349
00:27:42,310 --> 00:27:44,000
Excuse me.

350
00:27:44,810 --> 00:27:51,500
If my father asks to speak with me,
please do not let him through.

351
00:27:52,310 --> 00:27:55,120
He may have sent that man after me.

352
00:27:55,120 --> 00:27:57,270
Your own father?

353
00:27:57,270 --> 00:28:00,290
What makes you say that?

354
00:28:04,030 --> 00:28:08,920
I am searching for my missing sister.

355
00:28:08,920 --> 00:28:11,150
A sister...

356
00:28:11,150 --> 00:28:13,000
Can I get her name?

357
00:28:14,160 --> 00:28:16,450
Her name is Shiharu Nanase.

358
00:28:22,100 --> 00:28:26,830
Haruka Nanase. Can I confirm something?

359
00:28:26,830 --> 00:28:27,810
Yes, sir.

360
00:28:27,810 --> 00:28:33,250
Did you visit a Furukawa Clinic
the other day?

361
00:28:34,030 --> 00:28:35,280
Yes, sir.

362
00:28:35,280 --> 00:28:40,020
The director there is saying you ran amok,

363
00:28:40,020 --> 00:28:43,280
and injured one of their nurses.

364
00:28:43,280 --> 00:28:45,200
Is that true?

365
00:28:51,070 --> 00:28:55,170
Since they filed a report,
I'll have to ask about that, too.

366
00:28:56,870 --> 00:29:00,940
My father tried to forcibly have me admitted.

367
00:29:00,940 --> 00:29:03,350
I only acted in self defense.

368
00:29:03,350 --> 00:29:05,550
Let's get our stories straight.

369
00:29:06,360 --> 00:29:08,330
First of all.

370
00:29:09,770 --> 00:29:14,370
Why'd you break into Kayoko Senba's home?

371
00:29:18,980 --> 00:29:22,980
They suspect he's manipulating the market.

372
00:29:22,980 --> 00:29:24,940
So that's why surveillance is on his ass.

373
00:29:24,940 --> 00:29:28,750
I heard the Nichie stock is about to tank.

374
00:29:28,750 --> 00:29:30,150
Can anyone tell me more?

375
00:29:30,150 --> 00:29:33,230
Nichie? Their stock won't tank or rise.

376
00:29:33,230 --> 00:29:37,690
But I heard there was trouble
with the previous head?

377
00:29:37,690 --> 00:29:41,770
Oh yeah, wasn't someone looking into them?

378
00:29:41,770 --> 00:29:43,350
What was his name...

379
00:29:43,350 --> 00:29:45,900
Right, Hirama. From Toho Journal.

380
00:29:45,900 --> 00:29:49,310
Can you introduce me to him?

381
00:29:49,310 --> 00:29:50,930
He's actually here right now.

382
00:29:53,350 --> 00:29:56,980
Do you know anyone in Plantae?

383
00:29:56,980 --> 00:30:01,230
I want a lead, without our Chief finding out.

384
00:30:01,230 --> 00:30:03,480
Well...

385
00:30:03,480 --> 00:30:07,090
Mr. Hirama from Toho Journal, yes?

386
00:30:07,760 --> 00:30:12,210
Did you know a reporter
by the name of Onodera?

387
00:30:16,360 --> 00:30:18,480
Give us a minute.

388
00:30:18,480 --> 00:30:19,830
Yes, sir.

389
00:30:21,020 --> 00:30:24,690
And try to find someone, will you?

390
00:30:24,690 --> 00:30:26,390
Yeah, yeah.

391
00:30:28,830 --> 00:30:32,780
He came to me with questions
just the other day.

392
00:30:32,780 --> 00:30:33,980
[Yoichi Onodera]

393
00:30:33,980 --> 00:30:38,000
He wanted to ask about Nichie Pharmaceutical.

394
00:30:40,650 --> 00:30:44,830
What was Onodera looking into?

395
00:30:49,400 --> 00:30:53,950
Onodera mentioned the "Plantae" to me.

396
00:30:56,700 --> 00:30:59,290
I work as the Japanese representative

397
00:30:59,290 --> 00:31:02,230
for Xin Ming Ah, a Chinese conglomerate.

398
00:31:02,230 --> 00:31:04,220
The name is Kojima.

399
00:31:05,560 --> 00:31:10,950
I look into Japanese companies
Xin Ming Ah wishes to buy out.

400
00:31:11,770 --> 00:31:13,750
I see.

401
00:31:15,350 --> 00:31:19,480
So you plan to purchase
Nichie Pharmaceutical.

402
00:31:19,480 --> 00:31:23,690
That was the plan.
But we are currently at a standstill.

403
00:31:23,690 --> 00:31:25,370
Why is that?

404
00:31:29,100 --> 00:31:33,910
Share with me whatever you know.

405
00:31:34,570 --> 00:31:40,420
And I will offer my intel to you.

406
00:31:48,340 --> 00:31:51,400
Why hasn't the buy out occurred yet?

407
00:31:51,400 --> 00:31:55,750
There was a suspicious exchange of money.

408
00:31:56,870 --> 00:32:00,660
<i>We first visited Nichie last month.</i>

409
00:32:04,060 --> 00:32:10,080
We, Xin Ming Ah, plan to buy out
Nichie Pharmaceutical.

410
00:32:12,980 --> 00:32:15,300
Bring up the other matter as well.

411
00:32:16,740 --> 00:32:22,560
However, we have refrained
from taking action after noticing

412
00:32:22,560 --> 00:32:24,830
a discrepancy in your financial statements.

413
00:32:26,310 --> 00:32:28,270
Your budget for developing medicines

414
00:32:28,270 --> 00:32:31,580
increases during a certain period of time.

415
00:32:31,580 --> 00:32:33,300
Impossible.

416
00:32:34,440 --> 00:32:38,330
I've brought the result
of my investigation right here.

417
00:32:39,650 --> 00:32:41,080
You there.

418
00:32:42,190 --> 00:32:44,200
Bring these to your President.

419
00:32:51,940 --> 00:32:55,620
Shall I help? I know they are heavy.

420
00:33:05,230 --> 00:33:07,620
Sir.

421
00:33:16,770 --> 00:33:18,410
I see.

422
00:33:20,060 --> 00:33:25,060
These are documents
from my father's time as President.

423
00:33:25,060 --> 00:33:26,520
Indeed.

424
00:33:26,520 --> 00:33:28,480
I understand.

425
00:33:28,480 --> 00:33:34,300
We shall look into it,
and reach out again after some discussion.

426
00:33:39,600 --> 00:33:41,950
Please do.

427
00:33:44,960 --> 00:33:48,950
Since reporting our findings,
they've begun to make an effort

428
00:33:48,950 --> 00:33:52,310
to get rid of all associated evidence.

429
00:33:52,310 --> 00:33:55,650
A buy out would bring their secrets to light.

430
00:33:55,650 --> 00:33:57,270
I suppose that was their biggest fear.

431
00:33:57,270 --> 00:34:01,100
Indeed.

432
00:34:01,100 --> 00:34:06,620
Then Nichie Pharmaceutical
is hiding something after all.

433
00:34:09,360 --> 00:34:11,390
This is the last of it.

434
00:34:11,390 --> 00:34:15,860
If you find anything else, dispose it,
or hand the data directly to me.

435
00:34:15,860 --> 00:34:17,310
Do not send it over in any way.

436
00:34:17,310 --> 00:34:18,950
Yes, sir.

437
00:34:22,000 --> 00:34:23,330
Hello?

438
00:34:26,400 --> 00:34:28,250
Right now?

439
00:34:42,450 --> 00:34:49,090
Your father requested I deliver you
a change of clothes, and other necessities.

440
00:34:49,090 --> 00:34:52,500
You will find them with the receptionist.

441
00:34:53,940 --> 00:34:55,790
Is that all?

442
00:35:01,850 --> 00:35:03,940
Your father worries about you.

443
00:35:03,940 --> 00:35:06,520
Please do not come again.

444
00:35:06,520 --> 00:35:09,060
I do not need any more "necessities".

445
00:35:09,060 --> 00:35:10,800
Is that so.

446
00:35:12,560 --> 00:35:13,740
Why were you attacked?

447
00:35:13,740 --> 00:35:16,000
That's none of your business.

448
00:35:17,600 --> 00:35:19,600
Are you looking into the missing bones?

449
00:35:19,600 --> 00:35:22,250
Do they interest you?

450
00:35:24,490 --> 00:35:27,000
No, rather...

451
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:31,820
Your father, he worries for you.

452
00:35:33,360 --> 00:35:37,160
I know he had Dr. Furukawa
file a complaint.

453
00:35:37,990 --> 00:35:40,410
Why would he do that?

454
00:35:41,190 --> 00:35:44,650
To keep me shackled here.

455
00:35:44,650 --> 00:35:47,540
He doesn't want me looking into those bones.

456
00:35:55,020 --> 00:35:58,750
Why don't you accept your father's help,
and have him give you a job?

457
00:36:01,660 --> 00:36:04,160
He almost killed me.

458
00:36:05,280 --> 00:36:09,940
Your father is worried Professor Ishimizaki
got you involved in some trouble.

459
00:36:09,940 --> 00:36:11,430
He said you were in danger.

460
00:36:11,430 --> 00:36:14,190
And now you have been attacked.

461
00:36:14,190 --> 00:36:17,020
How is any of that your father's fault?

462
00:36:17,020 --> 00:36:21,750
To me, it seems you alone
are creating a fuss out of nothing.

463
00:36:24,560 --> 00:36:28,900
You are blessed, you know that?

464
00:36:28,900 --> 00:36:32,680
Think back to your life
before your mother remarried.

465
00:36:39,000 --> 00:36:41,140
What do you know about me?

466
00:36:45,280 --> 00:36:51,000
I grew up with similar circumstances.

467
00:36:53,100 --> 00:36:58,940
I have killed my own desires
to claw my way to this position.

468
00:36:58,940 --> 00:37:02,380
Yet my orders are
to bring you a change of clothes.

469
00:37:03,570 --> 00:37:06,440
You hit the jackpot
thanks to your parents' remarriage.

470
00:37:06,440 --> 00:37:10,220
You have people bringing you things,
despite the trouble you've caused.

471
00:37:11,950 --> 00:37:15,410
You'd be a fool to discard
the hand you've been dealt.

472
00:37:21,400 --> 00:37:24,320
If you need anything, call me.

473
00:37:24,320 --> 00:37:26,630
I can't trust my father.

474
00:37:29,070 --> 00:37:31,950
He's hiding something big from me.

475
00:37:35,210 --> 00:37:36,840
Is that so.

476
00:37:44,610 --> 00:37:47,480
This is Kasuga, speaking.

477
00:37:47,480 --> 00:37:49,600
I hope you are faring well.

478
00:37:49,600 --> 00:37:53,440
Did you tell Haruka Nanase anything?

479
00:37:53,440 --> 00:37:59,190
You wouldn't speak of "log.0", would you?

480
00:37:59,190 --> 00:38:01,000
And can I be absolutely certain?

481
00:38:01,730 --> 00:38:04,010
Me, speak of that?

482
00:38:04,850 --> 00:38:07,000
No, of course not.

483
00:38:07,000 --> 00:38:09,470
Why would you even ask?

484
00:38:10,750 --> 00:38:15,670
I believe I met every demand you asked me of.

485
00:38:16,400 --> 00:38:18,850
If you find any issues,

486
00:38:18,850 --> 00:38:22,100
I ask that you deal with it yourselves.

487
00:38:54,620 --> 00:38:56,130
Get in.

488
00:39:37,480 --> 00:39:39,190
Shiharu.

489
00:39:39,190 --> 00:39:41,760
You can't leave without telling anyone.

490
00:39:50,040 --> 00:39:51,750
We're going home.

491
00:39:52,330 --> 00:39:54,590
Why?

492
00:39:54,590 --> 00:39:56,790
They look like they're having so much fun.

493
00:39:59,210 --> 00:40:02,540
Dad doesn't want you wandering around.

494
00:40:02,540 --> 00:40:03,910
Come on, let's go.

495
00:40:23,900 --> 00:40:26,700
I was chased out the house.

496
00:40:26,700 --> 00:40:29,560
You idiot. Let me tell you.

497
00:40:29,560 --> 00:40:33,540
You weren't chased out
'cause you're a stupid drunk.

498
00:40:34,950 --> 00:40:36,660
Again?

499
00:40:36,660 --> 00:40:38,640
I'm going to get closer.

500
00:40:38,640 --> 00:40:40,480
Don't.

501
00:40:40,480 --> 00:40:41,740
Shiharu.

502
00:40:41,740 --> 00:40:44,300
- I'll open it.
- No, I will.

503
00:40:44,300 --> 00:40:45,980
Woah!

504
00:40:45,980 --> 00:40:47,410
Careful now...

505
00:40:47,410 --> 00:40:50,100
Thanks, miss.

506
00:40:50,100 --> 00:40:51,790
Why don't you join us?

507
00:40:51,790 --> 00:40:54,970
Yeah, come here.

508
00:40:54,970 --> 00:40:57,580
What were you all talking about?

509
00:40:57,580 --> 00:41:01,270
Hear this! Apparently this guy
hates herring roe.

510
00:41:01,270 --> 00:41:02,950
I don't like it either.

511
00:41:02,950 --> 00:41:04,850
See? I have an ally.

512
00:41:04,850 --> 00:41:06,830
You've just never had the real thing.

513
00:41:06,830 --> 00:41:09,230
- Exactly.
- Well, I don't care.

514
00:41:09,230 --> 00:41:11,440
This girl's got the right idea.

515
00:41:11,440 --> 00:41:12,500
I know.

516
00:41:12,500 --> 00:41:14,850
But real herring roe's delicious.

517
00:41:14,850 --> 00:41:18,410
You just haven't tried the right thing.

518
00:41:18,410 --> 00:41:20,530
I'll buy some next time.

519
00:41:20,530 --> 00:41:21,830
The salted stuff.

520
00:41:21,830 --> 00:41:25,860
It's good. Sweet, too.

521
00:41:25,860 --> 00:41:27,750
Really?

522
00:41:31,410 --> 00:41:33,410
They gotta be in the right condition.

523
00:41:33,410 --> 00:41:37,230
You split the belly,

524
00:41:37,230 --> 00:41:39,520
and out pops the roe!

525
00:41:39,520 --> 00:41:42,700
It pops right out!

526
00:41:50,690 --> 00:41:54,710
It's quiet.

527
00:41:59,850 --> 00:42:02,160
Maybe today's not a drinking day.

528
00:42:04,480 --> 00:42:06,410
No.

529
00:42:13,980 --> 00:42:19,540
Some people are just made to never exist.

530
00:42:21,570 --> 00:42:25,370
No one cares if they disappear.

531
00:42:26,120 --> 00:42:28,370
That's an awful thing to say.

532
00:42:29,470 --> 00:42:32,080
I wasn't talking about those men.

533
00:42:49,350 --> 00:42:50,770
They've got questions for you.

534
00:42:50,770 --> 00:42:52,120
Follow me.

535
00:42:53,900 --> 00:42:56,750
Were you able to sleep?

536
00:43:03,240 --> 00:43:08,250
First, I wish to speak in regards
to Professor Ishimizaki's daughter.

537
00:43:08,980 --> 00:43:12,460
Mari? Has she been found?

538
00:43:15,650 --> 00:43:17,500
Yes, well...

539
00:43:18,470 --> 00:43:21,330
She was taken in by relatives

540
00:43:21,330 --> 00:43:24,790
right after Professor Ishimizaki's passing.
She is safe.

541
00:43:30,140 --> 00:43:34,410
I was told she went missing.

542
00:43:46,770 --> 00:43:52,510
I have one more thing to tell you.

543
00:43:57,540 --> 00:44:00,750
Please do not panic when I say this.

544
00:44:07,020 --> 00:44:11,900
Your younger sister, Shiharu Nanase,

545
00:44:11,900 --> 00:44:14,670
does not exist.

546
00:44:24,730 --> 00:44:27,230
She died?

547
00:44:27,230 --> 00:44:29,410
- No.
- Where?

548
00:44:32,940 --> 00:44:34,510
Why?

549
00:44:36,790 --> 00:44:38,900
Why did she die?

550
00:44:38,900 --> 00:44:42,540
- Tell me, please!
- Calm down!

551
00:44:47,110 --> 00:44:50,450
According to our findings,

552
00:44:50,450 --> 00:44:53,160
you never had a younger sister.

553
00:45:03,750 --> 00:45:05,620
What?

554
00:45:05,620 --> 00:45:08,010
She never existed in the first place.

555
00:45:11,810 --> 00:45:13,830
What are you talking about?

556
00:45:14,900 --> 00:45:18,560
Your father has confirmed it.

557
00:45:18,560 --> 00:45:21,150
We checked your family register as well.

558
00:45:21,150 --> 00:45:24,950
No woman named Shiharu Nanase existed.

559
00:45:43,380 --> 00:45:45,500
What are you talking about?
